Found the bug — the connected correlation predicts `(π/N)²·(S_Q(h)−1)`, not `(π/N)²·S_Q(h)`. The −1 subtracts the q=1 disconnected piece (which lives in `mean²`). For h=2, Q=30 the ratio is 0.985 with the corrected formula. Let me update the code and re-run.
