t rules; this is correct policy not an omission. **A-grade scarcity escalated**: S147 flagged 0/N; S163 flagged 0/20; S192 flagged 0/30; **S201 flags 0/40 across four consecutive critique-windows**. The frontier-saturation pattern persists at maximal severity: every wild_swing closes at mode E or I via classical-result-citation closures (E7.21 = Pólya-Carlson + finite-singularity D-finite + Furstenberg-Lipshitz). The harness has continued to select commit/refinement/paradigm-shift modes despite four critique-window recommendations to attempt §A.A7 plethysm sub-frame OR §D.D48 BC endomotive Galois-orbit (highest-A-prior open vectors with un-imported cross-domain ingredients). **Recommended next-action**: (1) §A.A7 plethysm sub-frame (cost 2-3 sessions; first session can compute plethysm coefficients for n=4,5 via SYMMETRICA); (2) §D.D48 BC endomotive Galois-orbit (cost 1-2 sessions, distinct from CCM spectral triple at S53/E3.1); (3) housekeeping — Thread 2 WRAP slot 5/5 synthesis if commit fires (C-grade, .commit_state hygiene). **Meta-pattern escalation**: this is the **fourth** consecutive critique flagging the same A-grade scarcity issue without harness response. The framework is producing disciplined honest B-grade work but no breakthrough attempts have been selected. CLAUDE.md "≥ 2 F-grade sessions" escalation threshold NOT hit, but four-window recurrence of same recommendation is a meta-pattern exceeding normal CLAUDE.md tolerance — flagged for user awareness. **No edits to EDGES.md, NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md, ATTACK_VECTORS.md, RESEARCH_AGENDA.md, or CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md** (no demotions; A7/D48 recommendations are continuations of S163/S192 picks). See `archive/ephemeral/critique_latest.md`, `archive/sessions/session201_critique.md`. | 201 |
